    "id": 133,
    "question": "An international aviation cargo terminal must comply with the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) codifications under 49 CFR Part 1542. The facility's security director is evaluating an upgrade to the security identification display area (SIDA) access points. If a biometric retinal scanning system is selected, what secondary physical control must be integrated into the portal to prevent \"piggybacking\" or \"tailgating\" by unauthorized personnel attempting to follow a cleared individual?",
    "answer": "The retinal scanner must be integrated into a physical mantrap interlocking vestibule system (smart capsule). The mantrap must feature two doors that are electronically interlocked so that Door B cannot unlock until Door A has closed and locked, and a successful single-user biometric authentication has been verified inside the enclosure. To prevent piggybacking (two people entering on one credential), the interior of the mantrap must be equipped with overhead automated volumetric sensors or weight-sensing floor mats calibrated to detect the presence of more than one individual. If an anomaly is detected, both doors lock completely, an alarm is transmitted to the Security Operations Center, and the portal remains secured until human security officers physically clear the zone.",
