    "id": 149,
    "question": "A commercial port facility must comply with the Maritime Transportation Security Act (MTSA) and the International Ship and Port Facility Security (ISPS) Code. The facility security officer (FSO) receives intelligence indicating an elevated threat level (MTSA MarSec Level 2). What specific adjustments must be made to the facility's physical access control screening rates and perimeter patrol frequencies to maintain regulatory compliance?",
    "answer": "Upon escalation to MarSec Level 2, the FSO must immediately implement the additional protective measures outlined in the facility’s approved security plan. This mandates an increase in the frequency and intensity of physical access screenings: for example, upgrading from a baseline random 5% vehicle and personnel inspection rate to a mandatory 20% or 50% screening rate at all active access gates. Perimeter security must be tightened by increasing the frequency of mobile waterborne and shoreside patrols, locking down secondary or non-essential access portals entirely, establishing restricted zones adjacent to vessels, and intensifying continuous CCTV monitoring of the waterside boundaries to detect unauthorized approaches by small watercraft.",
