    "id": 162,
    "question": "A corporate executive protection (EP) detail is planning a high-profile public appearance for a CEO at an open-air urban amphitheater. The detail leader must mitigate the threat of a standoff weapon attack from elevated vantage points surrounding the venue. What specific tactical planning tool must be generated during the advance site survey, and what operational deployment is required to cover un-cleared high zones?",
    "answer": "The advance detail must generate a comprehensive \"line-of-sight (LOS) analysis map\" or \"vulnerability sector overlay\" that identifies every elevated platform, roof, window, or structural vantage point within the maximum effective range of a high-powered rifle targeting the stage area. To mitigate threats from these zones, the EP detail must deploy static counter-surveillance observers or designated marksman units on dominant high ground positions to monitor the un-cleared sectors. Concurrently, they must utilize structural countermeasures at the venue, such as erecting opaque ballistic screening panels or heavy architectural banners to physically block the line of sight between the executive's position and the identified high-risk elevated vantage points.",
