    "question": "What constitute the essential regulatory components and retention standards for corporate security documentation during an incident involving a serious workplace injury under OSHA 300, 300A, and 301 reporting frameworks?",
    "answer": "When a recordable workplace injury occurs, the corporate security or safety officer must log the incident on the OSHA Form 300 (Log of Work-Related Injuries and Illnesses) within seven calendar days of receiving information. A detailed narrative of the incident must be recorded on OSHA Form 301 (Injury and Illness Incident Report). Annually, the employer must compile and display the OSHA Form 300A (Summary of Work-Related Injuries and Illnesses) in a conspicuous employee area from February 1 to April 30. All of these forms, along with supporting security incident reports and witness statements, must be retained within the corporate archives for a mandatory minimum period of five years following the end of the calendar year that they cover, accessible for unannounced inspections by federal safety compliance officers.",
