    "question": "A US commercial real estate management firm experiences an extortion threat from an anonymous actor who claims to have compromised the Building Automation System (BAS) of a 40-story office tower, threatening to shut down all HVAC systems during a record heatwave if a cryptocurrency ransom is not paid. What immediate containment and forensic steps must the facility security manager execute?",
    "answer": "The security manager must immediately transition all building control systems from digital network control to local manual override modes at the physical control panels, effectively isolating the HVAC, electrical, and water systems from the compromised IP network. The manager must establish a unified incident command including corporate IT security, BAS vendor engineers, and federal law enforcement (FBI Cyber Division). Security teams must preserve all firewall traffic logs, router configurations, and BAS server memory states without rebooting the systems, locate the network ingress point used by the attacker, revoke all external VPN and remote-desktop credentials, and sequentially scan and re-verify the firmware integrity of all programmable logic controllers (PLCs) before bringing the systems back online on a strictly segmented, firewalled network layer.",
