    "question": "Under the Emergency Planning and Community Right-to-Know Act (EPCRA), what mandatory reporting obligations do US facilities have regarding the storage of Extremely Hazardous Substances (EHS) above specified Threshold Planning Quantities (TPQ)?",
    "answer": "Under EPCRA Sections 302 and 303, any facility storing an EHS in an amount equal to or greater than its designated TPQ must notify the State Emergency Response Commission (SERC) and the Local Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC) within 60 days of the substance reaching that threshold. Furthermore, under Sections 311 and 312, the facility must submit annual chemical inventory reporting forms—known as Tier II reports—to the SERC, LEPC, and the local jurisdictional fire department by March 1 of each year, detailing the chemical names, maximum quantities on-site, storage conditions, and exact physical locations within the facility to ensure local first responders can prepare adequate tactical response and evacuation plans for a chemical release emergency.",
