    "question": "During a formal corporate interview of an executive suspecting of massive procurement fraud, the subject suddenly stops speaking, displays intense physiological stress markers, and requests to leave the room. How should the corporate investigator manage this critical point in the interview without violating US labor laws or creating civil liability?",
