    "answer": "To meet PIV-I compliance, a contractor must execute a two-step identity verification process requiring two forms of official identification, one of which must be a federal or state government-issued photo ID, verified against authoritative databases. The physical credential must contain an integrated circuit chip storing an asymmetric X.509 cryptographic certificate issued by a certificate authority chained directly to the Federal Policy Management Authority (FPMA) root. For facility access control, the system must perform a real-time Challenge-Response authentication handshake using the PIV authentication key over the contactless interface, ensuring the credential cannot be cloned, skimmed, or bypassed via a replay attack.",
