    "answer": "Negligent hiring occurs when an employer fails to exercise reasonable care in checking an applicant's background before hiring them, resulting in placing an unfit individual in a position where they can harm others. Negligent retention occurs when an employer becomes aware, or should have become aware through reasonable supervision, that an existing employee has demonstrated dangerous, unstable, or unfit behavior during their employment, yet the employer fails to take corrective action, reassign, or terminate the individual. If that employee subsequently causes harm to a third party, the employer is directly liable for their independent failure to manage a known risk.",
