    "question": "What are the explicit legal protections afforded to whistleblowers under the Sarbanes-Oxley Act (SOX) Section 806, and what administrative body handles the initial filing of a retaliation complaint?",
    "answer": "SOX Section 806 protects employees of publicly traded companies who report internal corporate fraud, securities violations, or mail/wire fraud to federal regulatory bodies, law enforcement, members of Congress, or a supervisor within the corporation. It prohibits employers from discharging, demoting, suspending, threatening, or harassing the whistleblower. The initial administrative complaint must be filed with the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), a division of the U.S. Department of Labor (DOL), within 180 days of the retaliatory action. If OSHA does not issue a final decision within 210 days, the whistleblower has the right to bring a de novo action in federal district court for reinstatement, back pay with interest, and compensation for special damages.",
