    "question": "In emergency management planning, define the technical operational functions of a Joint Information Center (JIC) and its relationship to the Public Information Officer (PIO) under the National Incident Management System (NIMS).",
    "answer": "Under NIMS, the Public Information Officer (PIO) is responsible for interfacing with the public and media, managing incident communications, and drafting official statements. When an incident expands to involve multiple agencies or jurisdictions, a Joint Information Center (JIC) is established as a physical or virtual collaborative facility. The JIC co-locates PIOs from all participating public and private organizations to ensure a unified message. Its primary operational function is to eliminate conflicting public announcements, execute media monitoring to dispel rumors, and coordinate the distribution of verified, accurate information under a single, authoritative voice during a crisis.",
