    "question": "Define the technical mechanism and operational security function of a SIEM (Security Information and Event Management) system within a modern enterprise security operations center.",
    "answer": "A SIEM system operates by ingestion, normalization, and correlation of log data generated across an enterprise’s entire infrastructure—including firewalls, domain controllers, endpoints, access control databases, and cloud environments. Its primary technical mechanism is log aggregation paired with a real-time correlation engine that analyzes disparate events to detect complex attack patterns (e.g., a physical badge-in at a New York facility occurring simultaneously with a logical VPN login from an IP address in Europe—indicating a compromised credential). Its operational security function is to provide centralized situational awareness, eliminate alert fatigue by filtering noise, and automatically generate high-fidelity security alerts for rapid triage and incident response containment.",
