    "id": 499,
    "question": "A manufacturing corporation's primary IT data center is totally destroyed by a catastrophic electrical fire. The BCP specifies a failover to a cold site facility. Outline the operational sequence and resource allocations required by the Disaster Recovery Team to activate and restore services at a cold site within a reasonable timeframe.",
    "answer": "Activating a cold site requires a labor-intensive, sequential recovery process because the facility provides only physical space, power, and cooling, with zero pre-installed hardware or data infrastructure. Step 1: Execute immediate emergency procurement and logistics to ship physical servers, networking switches, and storage arrays from pre-negotiated hardware vendors to the cold site location. Step 2: Deploy infrastructure engineers to physically install hardware, configure network routing, and re-establish secure communication links (VPNs/leased lines) to corporate branch offices. Step 3: Install base operating systems, hypervisors, and database management software from clean, verified software golden images. Step 4: Retrieve physical backup tapes or initiate cloud downloads of the most recent off-site data backups to restore data states, verify data integrity, and run validation scripts before routing live user traffic to the newly built environment.",
